14539	979	9	Materi Pertemuan Ke-9	Descriptive Text (Vocabulary Building and Poster)	2026-09-16	# [**LESSON PLAN**]()\n\n| &#xA;   Educational&#xA;   Institution&#xA;    | &#xA;   : MA YKUI Maskumambang&#xA;                                          |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| &#xA;  Phase/Grade/Semester&#xA;               | &#xA;  : F / XI / 1&#xA;  (Odd Semester)&#xA;                                |\n| &#xA;  Subject&#xA;                            | &#xA;  : English&#xA;                                                        |\n| &#xA;  Material&#xA;                           | &#xA;  : Descriptive&#xA;  Text&#xA;                                         |\n| &#xA;  Topic&#xA;                              | &#xA;  : Describing&#xA;  Environmental Problems and Waste Management&#xA;   |\n| &#xA;  Lesson&#xA;                             | &#xA;  : 9&#xA;                                                              |\n| &#xA;  Time Allocation&#xA;                    | &#xA;  : 80 minutes&#xA;  (2 periods)&#xA;                                   |\n| &#xA;  Teaching Implementation&#xA;            | &#xA;  :&#xA;                                                                |\n\n## [**A. LEARNING OUTCOMES**]()\n\nStudents are able to understand and produce spoken and written texts in the form of descriptive texts to describe objects, situations, or conditions, as well as convey information and recommendations appropriately, coherently, and communicatively.\n\n## [**B. LEARNING OBJECTIVES**]()\n\n1.     Students are able to identify information and vocabulary related to the environment and waste problems.\n\n2.     Students are able to describe pictures related to environmental conditions using appropriate vocabulary and sentence structures.\n\n3.     Students are able to give recommendations based on the situations shown in the pictures.\n\n4.     Students are able to understand the characteristics, structure, and communicative purpose of a poster.\n\n5.     Students are able to work collaboratively to create a poster about waste management using clear and communicative English.\n\n## [**C. MEANINGFUL UNDERSTANDING**]()\n\nThe ability to describe a situation clearly helps us communicate information to others. By understanding waste problems and appropriate waste management, students can use English to provide information, give recommendations, and encourage others to protect the environment.\n\n## [**D. LEARNING ACTIVITIES**]()\n\n| &#xA;   Stage of&#xA;   Learning&#xA;               | &#xA;   Learning&#xA;   Activities&#xA;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| &#xA;  Introduction&#xA;                            | &#xA;  1.    &#xA;  Students and the teacher pray before&#xA;  starting the lesson.  &#xA;  2.    &#xA;  The teacher checks students’&#xA;  attendance and readiness to learn.&#xA;  3.    &#xA;  The teacher conducts a brainstorming&#xA;  activity by showing several pictures related to environmental conditions.  &#xA;  4.    &#xA;  The teacher asks: “What can you&#xA;  see in the picture?” and “What do you think about the situation?”  &#xA;  5.    &#xA;  The teacher gives an overview of&#xA;  the lesson and explains the learning objectives.  &#xA;                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| &#xA;  Learning&#xA;  Cycle 1: Exploring&#xA;       | &#xA;  1.    &#xA;  The teacher displays several&#xA;  pictures showing environmental conditions and waste problems.  &#xA;  2.    &#xA;  Students observe the pictures and&#xA;  identify the objects, conditions, activities, and problems they can see.  &#xA;  3.    &#xA;  Students orally describe the&#xA;  pictures.&#xA;  4.    &#xA;  Students give recommendations&#xA;  based on the situations shown in the pictures, for example: “People should&#xA;  throw the bottles into the recycling bin.” / “We should keep the river&#xA;  clean.”&#xA;  5.    &#xA;  The teacher provides feedback on&#xA;  students’ pronunciation, vocabulary, grammar, and the relevance of their&#xA;  descriptions and recommendations.&#xA;   |\n| &#xA;  Learning&#xA;  Cycle 2: Planning&#xA;        | &#xA;  1.    &#xA;  Students participate in a listening&#xA;  activity. The teacher plays or reads a short text &#xA;  2.    &#xA;  Students listen to the text and&#xA;  complete the missing words in the worksheet. &#xA;  &#xA;  3.    &#xA;  The teacher and students discuss&#xA;  the answers together.  &#xA;  4.    &#xA;  Students then learn about kinds of&#xA;  waste and waste management.&#xA;  5.    &#xA;  Students classify different&#xA;  examples of waste into the appropriate categories.&#xA;                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| &#xA;  Learning&#xA;  Cycle 3: Doing&#xA;           | &#xA;  1.    &#xA;  The teacher explains the&#xA;  definition, purpose, characteristics, and elements of a poster.  &#xA;  2.    &#xA;  The teacher shows an example of an&#xA;  environmental poster and asks students to identify its title, slogan,&#xA;  images, information, and recommendation/call to action.  &#xA;  3.    &#xA;  Students are divided into several&#xA;  groups.  &#xA;  4.    &#xA;  Each group chooses one of the&#xA;  topics discussed, such as plastic waste, organic waste, recycling, waste&#xA;  sorting, reducing waste, or keeping the environment clean.  &#xA;  5.    &#xA;  Students work collaboratively to&#xA;  create an English poster.&#xA;                                                     |\n| &#xA;  Learning&#xA;  Cycle 4: Communicating&#xA;   | &#xA;  1.    &#xA;  Each group displays and presents&#xA;  its completed poster.  &#xA;  2.    &#xA;  Students explain the content of&#xA;  their poster, the waste problem they have chosen, and the solutions or recommendations&#xA;  they propose.  &#xA;  3.    &#xA;  Other groups observe the posters&#xA;  and give simple comments or questions. &#xA;  &#xA;  4.    &#xA;  The teacher provides feedback on&#xA;  the content, use of English, creativity, and relevance of the posters to the&#xA;  topic of waste management.&#xA;                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| &#xA;  Learning&#xA;  Cycle 5: Reflecting&#xA;      | &#xA;  1.    &#xA;  Students reflect on the knowledge&#xA;  and skills they have learned.&#xA;  2.    &#xA;  The teacher asks reflective&#xA;  questions: “What kind of waste do you find most often around you?” and&#xA;  “What can you do to reduce waste?” &#xA;  &#xA;  3.    &#xA;  The teacher reinforces the idea that&#xA;  English can be used to communicate information and encourage others to take&#xA;  positive action to protect the environment.&#xA;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| &#xA;  Closing&#xA;  &#xA;   &#xA;                  | &#xA;  1.    &#xA;  The teacher and students review&#xA;  the material they have learned.&#xA;  2.    &#xA;  The teacher reinforces the Meaningful&#xA;  Understanding about the importance of describing problems and&#xA;  communicating solutions through English.&#xA;  3.    &#xA;  The teacher appreciates and gives&#xA;  positive feedback on the students’ group work.&#xA;  4.    &#xA;  The teacher gives a preview of the&#xA;  next lesson.&#xA;  5.    &#xA;  The teacher and students pray&#xA;  after the lesson.&#xA;                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n\n## [**E. ASSESSMENT**]()\n\n### [1.     Attitude Assessment]()\n\nObservation of:\n\n·       Participation and engagement.\n\n·       Cooperation within the group.\n\n·       Responsibility in completing tasks.\n\n·       Confidence in expressing ideas.\n\n### [2.     Knowledge Assessment]()\n\nAssessment through:\n\n·       Listening comprehension.\n\n·       Identification of kinds of waste.\n\n·       Understanding of waste management.\n\n·       Understanding of the elements of a poster.\n\n### [3.     Skills Assessment]()\n\n**Group Poster Project**\n\n| &#xA;   Aspect&#xA;                         | &#xA;   Criteria&#xA;                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| &#xA;  Content&#xA;                         | &#xA;  Information is relevant to the topic of waste management.&#xA;   |\n| &#xA;  Language&#xA;                        | &#xA;  English is accurate and communicative.&#xA;                      |\n| &#xA;  Organization&#xA;                    | &#xA;  Information and messages are clearly organized.&#xA;             |\n| &#xA;  Creativity&#xA;                      | &#xA;  The poster is creative and visually appealing.&#xA;              |\n| &#xA;  Recommendation/Call to Action&#xA;   | &#xA;  Contains a clear recommendation or call to action.&#xA;          |\n| &#xA;  Presentation&#xA;                    | &#xA;  The group can explain the poster clearly.&#xA;                   |\n\n## [F. LEARNING MEDIA]()\n\n1.     English textbook.\n\n2.     Pictures showing environmental conditions.\n\n3.     Listening audio/text.\n\n4.     Poster paper/cardboard.\n\n5.     Markers, colored pencils, and other supporting materials.\n\n6.     LCD/Projector.
